cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use crashmetrics in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "crashmetrics: Python tools for automotive crash engineering metrics"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Voonna"
    given-names: "Satish Kumar"
version: "0.15.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23806423
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vsk1729/crashmetrics"
url: "https://vsk1729.github.io/crashmetrics/"
abstract: >-
  Open-source Python package for automotive crash safety calculations:
  injury criteria (HIC, Nij, BrIC, DAMAGE, chest and leg criteria),
  Euro NCAP scoring (frontal, sled and virtual testing, side, far side,
  whiplash), Bharat NCAP
  adult and child occupant scoring and star rating, pedestrian protection, homologation
  checks (UN R94, R95, R135, AIS-098, AIS-099, AIS-100, post-crash
  electrical safety), intrusion measurement, LS-DYNA ASCII output
  readers and energy checks,
  test-versus-CAE correlation (ISO/TS 18571, corridor and
  cross-correlation), feature extraction, design of experiments,
  sensitivity ranking and probabilistic ratings for machine learning.
keywords:
  - crashworthiness
  - crash safety
  - injury criteria
  - Euro NCAP
  - Bharat NCAP
  - pedestrian protection
  - LS-DYNA
  - CAE
